From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: apps not needed at boot are held back

Boot completed waits for apps not needed at boot.

BOOT_COMPLETED started every app with a receiver for it at once. On
this 2.8 GB phone a trace of the first three minutes after boot showed
88 process starts (48 for broadcasts), 40 lowmemorykiller kills and up
to 75k workingset refaults per 10 s; Settings took 17 s to open.
MuditaOS avoids this with MediaTek's DuraSpeed, which suppresses
background starts; Android's own defer_boot_completed_broadcast is only
a constant in Android 16, nothing reads it.

BOOT_COMPLETED for the main user now goes at once to everyone except
manifest receivers in packages that are neither core (app id below
FIRST_APPLICATION_UID), persistent, nor on a short list (Play services
and Services Framework, Clock, Calendar and its provider, cell
broadcast, device config, LineageOS settings config). Those get it at
their first start, as private space packages already do, or otherwise
one every two seconds from two minutes after boot.

Apps held at boot are not started for background broadcasts.

0122 holds BOOT_COMPLETED back from apps not needed at boot, but the
same apps were still started in the first minutes by every other
broadcast: storage mounted, Bluetooth and network changes, widget
updates, pushes. Two boot traces of 382 showed 75-80 process starts
and 40-42 lowmemorykiller kills in three minutes.

While an app's BOOT_COMPLETED is held, a broadcast queue for one of its
uids with no running process is not runnable, unless it holds an
ordered, result-awaiting, alarm or interactive broadcast. The hold ends
with the BOOT_COMPLETED hold: when the app first starts for any other
reason (opened, a provider or a service) or at its turn two minutes
after boot. Nothing is dropped; queued broadcasts are delivered then.
